# Day 01 – 3-Tier Architecture

## 📌 Topic
3-Tier Architecture – Theory

## 📖 Explanation
3-Tier Architecture is a software design pattern that divides an application into three layers:
Presentation Layer, Application Layer, and Data Layer.
Each layer has a specific responsibility, which makes the application easy to manage and maintain.

## 🏗️ Layers Explanation

### 1. Presentation Layer
This is the user interface layer.
Users interact with this layer.
HTML, CSS, and JavaScript are used here.

### 2. Application Layer
This layer contains business logic.
It processes user requests and controls application flow.
Languages like Java, Python, and PHP are used.

### 3. Data Layer
This layer stores and manages data.
It communicates with databases like MySQL and MongoDB.

## 🔄 Working Flow
User → Presentation Layer → Application Layer → Data Layer → Response

## ✅ Conclusion
3-Tier Architecture helps in building secure, scalable, and well-organized applications.
HTML belongs to the Presentation Layer.

